@page "/tooltip"

<PageTitle>Tooltip</PageTitle>

<h1>Tooltip</h1>

<section class="demo-section">
    <p>
        A tooltip either wraps the thing it describes or points at it by selector. The bubble goes in
        the browser's top layer, so it is never clipped by an <code>overflow: hidden</code> ancestor and
        never loses a z-index argument.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="demo-section">
    <h2>1. Wrapping a control</h2>
    <Tooltip Text="Applies the change without closing the sheet." Placement="TooltipPlacement.Top">
        <ShinyButton Text="Apply" />
    </Tooltip>
    <p style="font-size:0.875rem;">
        The wrapper is <code>display: contents</code>, so it does not change how the button lays out.
        The default trigger is hover <em>or</em> focus, which is what makes it reachable by keyboard.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="demo-section">
    <h2>2. Placement</h2>
    <div style="display:flex; gap:10px; flex-wrap:wrap;">
        <Tooltip Text="Above" Placement="TooltipPlacement.Top"><ShinyButton Text="Top" /></Tooltip>
        <Tooltip Text="Below" Placement="TooltipPlacement.Bottom"><ShinyButton Text="Bottom" /></Tooltip>
        <Tooltip Text="To the left" Placement="TooltipPlacement.Left"><ShinyButton Text="Left" /></Tooltip>
        <Tooltip Text="To the right" Placement="TooltipPlacement.Right"><ShinyButton Text="Right" /></Tooltip>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:0.875rem;">
        Placement is a preference, not a promise: a side with no room flips to the opposite one, and the
        bubble is clamped to stay on screen while the tail slides along to keep pointing at the target.
        Scroll the page with one open and it follows.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="demo-section">
    <h2>3. Clipped containers</h2>
    <p style="font-size:0.875rem;">
        The box below has <code>overflow: hidden</code>. An in-tree popover would be cut off at its edge.
    </p>
    <div style="overflow:hidden; height:90px; border:1px solid var(--shiny-color-outline-variant, #ccc);
                border-radius:12px; padding:16px;">
        <Tooltip Text="Drawn in the top layer, so the box cannot clip it." Placement="TooltipPlacement.Bottom">
            <ShinyButton Text="Hover me" />
        </Tooltip>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="demo-section">
    <h2>4. Bound to state</h2>
    <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px; max-width:360px;">
        <ShinyButton id="tt-hint-target" Text="Nothing to save yet" Disabled="true" />
        <ShinyButton Text="Toggle the hint" Appearance="ButtonAppearance.Outlined" Clicked="@(_ => Toggle())" />
    </div>

    @* No content: it points at a selector and is driven entirely from state. *@
    <Tooltip Target="#tt-hint-target"
             Title="Why is this disabled?"
             Text="Make a change first. Click this hint to dismiss it."
             Placement="TooltipPlacement.Bottom"
             Trigger="TooltipTrigger.Manual"
             @bind-IsOpen="showHint"
             Clicked="OnHintClickedAsync" />

    <p><em>@status</em></p>
</section>

<section class="demo-section">
    <h2>5. Styled</h2>
    <Tooltip Title="Heads up"
             Text="A tooltip takes the theme's inverse surface by default; give it a colour and it takes that instead."
             Placement="TooltipPlacement.Top"
             Trigger="TooltipTrigger.Click"
             BubbleColor="#0F766E"
             TextColor="#FFFFFF"
             MaxWidth="240px">
        <ShinyButton Text="Custom colours" />
    </Tooltip>
</section>

@code {
    bool showHint;
    string status = "Hover, focus or click a control to see its tooltip.";

    void Toggle() => this.showHint = !this.showHint;

    Task OnHintClickedAsync()
    {
        this.status = "The bound tooltip was clicked, which raised Clicked and closed it.";
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }
}
